{"kind":{"type":"frontMatter","text":"title: \"A self-update relaunch loses the open tabs: UserDefaults is not flushed before the new process reads it\"\u000adate: 2026-09-20\u000acategory: runtime-errors\u000amodule: RcGitApp\u000aproblem_type: runtime_error\u000acomponent: frontend\u000asymptoms:\u000a  - \"Rebuild and Relaunch brings the app back with one empty window; the repository tabs that were open are gone\"\u000a  - \"Before 974d820: `defaults read com.timeturnback.rcgit.dev` still lists the tabs under `rc-git.openTabs` while the relaunched app shows none (current code: the key holds an empty or older list instead)\"\u000a  - \"A manual quit and launch restores the same tabs correctly; only the self-update path drops them\"\u000a  - \"No error is logged and the update window reports success\"\u000aroot_cause: async_timing\u000aresolution_type: code_fix\u000aseverity: medium\u000aframework_version: macos 26.6.2\u000arelated_components: [userdefaults, cfprefsd, app-lifecycle, self-update]\u000atags: [userdefaults, cfprefsd, synchronize, nsworkspace, openapplication, relaunch, self-update, cross-process, race-condition, state-handover]"},"runs":[],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":1},"runs":[{"text":"A self-update relaunch loses the open tabs: UserDefaults is not flushed before the new process reads it","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Problem","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Rebuild and Relaunch","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (dev bundle) and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Update rc-git","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (release bundle) save the open tabs, launch the new build, and terminate. The relaunched build came up with one empty window even though the tab list was in ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"UserDefaults","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" — because it read the list before the old process's write reached disk.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Symptoms","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The relaunched app shows a single empty window; the repository tabs are gone.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Before 974d820: ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"defaults read com.timeturnback.rcgit.dev","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" shows ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"rc-git.openTabs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" still holding the repository path. The value is intact; the new process simply did not see it. Under the current code the same race leaves the key holding an empty or older list instead (see \"Why This Works\").","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Quitting and launching by hand restores tabs correctly. Only the self-update path loses them.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Nothing is logged. The update window reports success.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"What Didn't Work","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The obvious suspect was the change shipped in the same session: ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"scripts/build-app.sh","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" had just started stamping ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"CFBundleShortVersionString","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" with the commit count, so the bundle's version string differed between the old and new build.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"That was ruled out by reading the domain rather than the code. ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"UserDefaults","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" is scoped by ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"CFBundleIdentifier","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", which ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"scripts/build-app.sh","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" stamps per variant and which no version change touches — and the dump proved the point directly: the tab list was ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"present","style":["emphasis"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" in the domain while the running app showed no tabs. A persistence bug cannot leave the value on disk. The failure was on the read side, not the write side.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Solution","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Flush the write before the replacement process launches, and stop writing once the state has been handed over.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"OpenTabs.handOff(live:selectedIndex:)","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"mac/Sources/RcGitKit/OpenTabs.swift","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"), as it reads today (it also logs whether the flush succeeded):","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"code","language":"swift","text":"public func handOff(live: [String], selectedIndex: Int) {\u000a    record(live: live, selectedIndex: selectedIndex)\u000a    defaults.synchronize()\u000a}"},"runs":[],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"AppDelegate.saveTabs(dropping:)","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"AppDelegate.handOffTabs()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"mac/Sources/RcGitApp/AppDelegate.swift","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"):","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"code","language":"swift","text":"func saveTabs(dropping: String? = nil) {\u000a    guard !tabsHandedOff else { return }\u000a    let state = tabState()\u000a    openTabs.record(\u000a        live: state.paths, selectedIndex: state.selectedIndex, dropping: dropping)\u000a}\u000a\u000afunc handOffTabs() {\u000a    let state = tabState()\u000a    openTabs.handOff(live: state.paths, selectedIndex: state.selectedIndex)\u000a    tabsHandedOff = true\u000a}"},"runs":[],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Both go through ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"OpenTabs.record","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", which merges the live tabs into the saved list, so a tab closed with ⇧⌘W or at ⌘Q stays in it; ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"OpenTabs.save","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" replaces the list and only ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"restoreTabs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" calls it (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".claude/rules/swift.md","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"). Do not swap ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"record","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" back to ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"save","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" here.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Fixed in commit ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"974d820","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" on ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"master","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", where the update window's ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"willRelaunch","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" closure called ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"handOffTabs()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" instead of ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"saveTabs()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":". Today ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"UpdateModel","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" calls ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"UpdateEnvironment.handOff()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", which ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"AppDelegate","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" wires to ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"handOffTabs()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"; when the launch fails it calls ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"UpdateEnvironment.reclaim()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", which runs ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"AppDelegate.reclaimTabs()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" to lift the latch and record the tabs again.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Why This Works","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"UpdateModel","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" relaunches in this order (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"UpdateEnvironmentLive","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" in ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"mac/Sources/RcGitApp/UpdateEnvironmentLive.swift","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" implements each step):","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"handOff()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" — save the tabs.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":{"ordered":1}},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"relaunch()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" — ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"NSWorkspace.shared.openApplication","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" with ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"createsNewApplicationInstance = true","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":{"ordered":2}},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"quit()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" — ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"NSApp.terminate(nil)","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":{"ordered":3}},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Between 2 and 3 ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"two processes of the same bundle identifier are alive at once","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", and the new one reads ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"rc-git.openTabs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" during ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"applicationDidFinishLaunching","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", milliseconds after step 1. A ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"UserDefaults","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" write is handed to ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"cfprefsd","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" asynchronously and committed to the domain's plist lazily; a process that starts fresh reads what was last committed. The new process therefore read a pre-save snapshot of the domain, found no tabs, and opened an empty window. ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"synchronize()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" forces the commit before the launch, which is exactly the cross-process handover case the method still exists for.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Why the value was nonetheless on disk afterwards, at the time of 974d820: ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"restoreTabs()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" returned without saving when it restored nothing, so the new process never clobbered the list; the old process then wrote it again from ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"applicationWillTerminate","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":". The symptom was a lost session, never a lost list — which is why the next manual launch looked fine and hid the bug.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"That no longer holds. ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"restoreTabs()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"mac/Sources/RcGitApp/AppDelegate.swift","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":") now always saves the list that ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"OpenTabs.restoredPaths","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" decides, also when nothing opened: the tabs that opened, then each repository that failed to open while its parent folder was unreachable (a volume not mounted yet). It drops a repository gone from a folder that exists and logs every failure under the ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"tabs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" category. And the old process's ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"saveTabs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" returns at ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"guard !tabsHandedOff","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" after the handover. So if the new process ever reads a stale list again, it writes that stale list (often empty) back and nothing rewrites the real one: the list is lost, not just the session.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"tabsHandedOff","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" closes the mirror image of the same window: the old process outlives the new one's launch, and its termination write would otherwise land on top of whatever the new process had already recorded.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Prevention","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"State handed to another process needs an explicit flush.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" Any ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"UserDefaults","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" value a second process reads while this one is still alive — a relaunch, a helper, an XPC service — must be ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"synchronize()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"d at the handover. ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"synchronize()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" is discouraged for ordinary saves and correct here; that is the distinction, not \"never call it\".","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"A handover is one-way.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" After handing state over, stop writing it. Two live processes writing one defaults domain is last-writer-wins, and the departing one usually writes last.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Read the domain before reading the code.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"defaults read <bundle-id>","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" separates a write bug from a read bug in one command. A value present on disk while the UI disagrees means the reader raced, not that persistence broke.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Under the current code a reader race does not leave the value behind.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" Right after a self-update, an empty or older ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"rc-git.openTabs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" is also consistent with the new process reading a stale domain: ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"restoreTabs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" saves what it restored even when nothing opened, and the old process stops writing after the handover. Check the ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"tabs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" log category for the ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"hand-off: flushed","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" line and the ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"restore tabs:","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" counts before blaming the write side.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Related: the bundle identifier is what scopes this state, which is why it must never depend on a version or build number (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"CLAUDE.md","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"docs/solutions/runtime-errors/appkit-swallowed-launch-exception-windowless-app.md","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" for the other launch-time failure in this app that also left no log trail).","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"}
],
